  "term": "MEG",
  "definition": "MEG, or magnetoencephalography, is a method for recording the very small magnetic fields generated by electrical activity in the brain, typically from outside the head with highly sensitive equipment. It helps show where brain activity is occurring and provides information that complements electroencephalography.",
